SUMMARY:Upper West Ridge - Walker's Knob - 8.8 Miles\, 2460 Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nAnother one on the harder side of 
 my usual hikes but we should have nice cool weather to keep us moving. Thi
 s is a repeat of a hike I did earlier this year but we will go in the oppo
 site direction and go to Walker's Knob instead of Graybeard Mtn. This is a
  rocky trail with some steep sections so please make sure you are capable 
 of doing this hike. We should be rewarded with some spectacular views and 
 hopefully the tailing fall colors. There will be some steep downhill secti
 ons. We will keep a moderate pace but stop as needed.\n\nhttps://www.alltr
 ails.com/explore/custom-routes/upper-west-ridge-walker-s-knob-a7a0a64\n\n*
 *CARPOOL**\nLet's meet at the Black Mountain Ingles at 8:30 on the McDonal
 ds side of the parking lot. There is very limited parking at the trailhead
  so try to carpool if possible. Use the Event Chat if you want to carpool 
 from Asheville.\n\n**WEATHER**\nThe weather currently might be okay for Mo
 nday but I'll watch the weather and post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM
  if there is a chance of severe weather or lightning during this time peri
 od..\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp or phone until t
 he hike starts although cell reception may be sketchy\, (508) 965-2333.\n\
 n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, pos
 sibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are respo
 nsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skil
 ls\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve 
 risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville H
 iking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants a
 ssume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
